ry device known as chekhov's gun  if the opening act prominently displays  a gun someone will shoot it during or  before the final act  godzilla vs kong's chekhov's gun comes  in the form of conspiracy theorist  bernie hayes alcohol  flask since the film draws attention to  the flask audiences know he will either  drink it or use it to save the day  but this chekhov's flask and its  contents also play double duty as an  easter egg when josh asks bernie what's  in the flask bernie says it is filled  with katsunari single malt whiskey  that's a very specific name for a  chekhov's gun did legendary pictures  make a deal with a whiskey manufacturer  to make bernie in his flask act as a  trojan  product placement no instead the name  most likely honors godzilla  film suit actor kazunari mori who played  mechagodzilla in 1974's godzilla vs  mechagodzilla so not only did the flask  and its contents tease how the main  villain will be defeated  its fictional brand name teases the  identity of said villain sure  the name of the whiskey isn't exactly  the same as the name of the original  mecha godzilla actor but it feels too  similar to just be a coincidence  since the godzilla franchise has been  around since 1954 the series has been  through  several ups and downs some more infamous  than others to godzilla fans it's  difficult to get more infamous than  north america's first attempt at  creating a godzilla film  that movie now wears a permanent  bullseye that godzilla vs kong's  creators gladly shot at  possibly during godzilla vs kong king  kong is trapped on a ship in the tasman  sea with miles of water in every  direction  he can't move but more importantly he  can't hunt for food  to mangle an old phrase what does a 158  ton gorilla eat  whatever he wants but since he's in the  middle of the ocean he'll just have to  settle for fish  a lot of fish one of the most frequently  derided scenes in the 1998 godzilla  movie is when the army tries to bait  godzilla out with fish  a big pile of fish  so kong's seafood feast in godzilla  versus kong is a fun callback to the  1998 box office disappointment  and finally though director adam wingard  formally crowns a winner in godzilla vs  kong the way the original matchup movie  didn't  he clearly still has love for the  original king kong vs godzilla  since the ending shots are very similar  in king kong vs godzilla kong swims away  as tiny humans watch from the shore  in godzilla vs kong it's godzilla who  swims away in a clear homage to the  original  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

